2026.TE34.108.s:
As the Toronto Transit Commission (TTC) operates a transit service on Queen Street West, City Council approval of this report is required.

SG Constructors is building a 27-storey residential condominium building at 1266 Queen St West. The site is located on the northeast corner of Queen Street West and Noble Street.

In order to facilitate construction staging operations for the development, Transportation Services is requesting authorization to implement the following temporary measures:

- Closure of the east sidewalk / boulevard and the northbound traffic lane on the east side of Noble Street, between Queen Street West and a point 85 metres north;

- Conversion of Noble Street from a two-way operation to a one-way traffic operation (northbound to westbound), between Queen Street West and Strickland Avenue;

- Installation of a stop control for westbound traffic on Noble Street and Strickland Avenue;

- Prohibit stopping at all times on both sides of Noble Street, between Queen Street West and a point 85 metres north;

- Prohibit stopping at all times on the north side of Queen Street West in the vicinity of the work zone.

The above temporary measures are required for a period of 24 months, from December 1, 2026 to November 30, 2028. During this period, pedestrian access on the east side of Noble Street adjacent to the site will be restricted. Pedestrians will be directed to use the sidewalk on the other side of Noble Street, with crossing opportunities provided at the stop-controlled intersections of Queen Street West and Noble Street, and Noble Street and Strickland Avenue.

